error[E0277]: `(u32, {integer})` is not ordered: the ordering operators are answered over the integer types only
  --> tests/ui/op_between_takes_a_pair.rs:13:48
   |
13 |     let _ = cipher.query(op::Lt, &(18u32, 65)).on(&age_plan);
   |                                                ^^ no ordering operator over this type
   |
   = help: the trait `Ordered` is not implemented for `(u32, {integer})`
   = note: `Lt`, `Lte`, `Gt`, `Gte` and `Between` take `u8` to `u128` or `i8` to `i128`; the order of text is not settled (ADR-0009), so an ordering over text does not compile
   = help: the following other types implement trait `Ordered`:
             i128
             i16
             i32
             i64
             i8
             u128
             u16
             u32
           and $N others
   = note: required for `Lt` to implement `DefaultIndex<(u32, {integer})>`
   = note: required for `ValuePlan<u32, Indexed<stack_encrypt::Ore>>` to implement `Chooses<Lt, (u32, {integer}), Whole>`
